["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>Your Tikka T3x Arctic has iron sights only. A good scope shows a deer clearly at dawn, for one clean shot.</p></aside>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Parts of a rifle scope, side view. Eyepiece at the back with the focus ring, then the power ring that zooms 3 to 9 times, the tube held by the rings, the elevation turret on top for up and down, the windage turret on the side for left and right, and the objective bell at the front with a 40 mm lens.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Parts of a scope: 3 to 9x40</text>\n  <!-- scope body -->\n  <path d=\"M20 128 L70 134 L70 166 L20 172 Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"70\" y=\"134\" width=\"44\" height=\"32\" fill=\"#4a4f48\"/>\n  <g stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><line x1=\"80\" y1=\"134\" x2=\"80\" y2=\"166\"/><line x1=\"90\" y1=\"134\" x2=\"90\" y2=\"166\"/><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"134\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"166\"/></g>\n  <rect x=\"114\" y=\"138\" width=\"170\" height=\"24\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <path d=\"M284 138 L320 118 L380 118 L380 182 L320 182 L284 162 Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"376\" y=\"122\" width=\"6\" height=\"56\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/>\n  <rect x=\"186\" y=\"108\" width=\"28\" height=\"30\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#4a4f48\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"150\" r=\"13\" fill=\"#4a4f48\" stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <!-- rings -->\n  <g fill=\"#8a9a6b\"><rect x=\"128\" y=\"134\" width=\"16\" height=\"44\"/><rect x=\"250\" y=\"134\" width=\"16\" height=\"44\"/></g>\n  <rect x=\"110\" y=\"178\" width=\"180\" height=\"8\" fill=\"#6b6f68\"/>\n  <!-- leaders -->\n  <g stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.2\">\n    <line x1=\"40\" y1=\"128\" x2=\"40\" y2=\"70\"/><line x1=\"92\" y1=\"134\" x2=\"110\" y2=\"94\"/><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"108\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"62\"/>\n    <line x1=\"350\" y1=\"118\" x2=\"350\" y2=\"70\"/><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"163\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"236\"/><line x1=\"136\" y1=\"178\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"236\"/>\n    <line x1=\"379\" y1=\"182\" x2=\"350\" y2=\"236\"/><line x1=\"160\" y1=\"186\" x2=\"160\" y2=\"276\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\n    <text x=\"44\" y=\"64\">Eyepiece</text><text x=\"116\" y=\"88\">Power ring 3 to 9</text>\n    <text x=\"200\" y=\"56\" fill=\"#e8590c\">Elevation: up, down</text>\n    <text x=\"340\" y=\"64\">Objective bell</text>\n    <text x=\"220\" y=\"252\" fill=\"#e8590c\">Windage: left, right</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"252\">Ring</text>\n    <text x=\"340\" y=\"252\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\">40 mm lens</text><text x=\"160\" y=\"292\">Rail on the rifle</text>\n  </g>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>A <strong>3 to 9x40</strong> or <strong>3.5 to 10x40</strong> covers BC deer to about 300 m <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>It must <strong>clear the rear drum sight</strong>: expect high rings (60 to 75%).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: budget and the full short answer</summary><ul><li>A <strong>3 to 9x40</strong> or <strong>3.5 to 10x40</strong> scope covers BC deer out to about 300 m <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Second focal plane, simple duplex crosshair, capped turrets (Tip).</li><li>Your Arctic has a tall rear drum sight. The scope must <strong>clear it</strong> <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Expect <strong>high rings</strong>, and dry fit before you pay <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li>Prices are in CAD (Canadian dollars).</li><li>Budget: entry about $270 to $690, mid about $765 to $1,300, premium about $1,700 to $3,300 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>. Price checked 2026-10-01.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Zoom compared. At 3 times power you see a wide view with the deer small among the trees, good for close deer in timber. At 9 times power the deer fills more of a narrow view, plenty for a deer at 300 metres.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Low power vs high power</text>\n  <!-- 3x -->\n  <circle cx=\"100\" cy=\"140\" r=\"86\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <g fill=\"#2f3a2b\"><polygon points=\"40,150 50,110 60,150\"/><polygon points=\"140,140 150,100 160,140\"/><polygon points=\"160,160 168,128 176,160\"/><polygon points=\"62,180 70,150 78,180\"/></g>\n  <g transform=\"translate(104 152)\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"><ellipse rx=\"10\" ry=\"5\"/><circle cx=\"9\" cy=\"-6\" r=\"3.5\"/><rect x=\"-8\" y=\"3\" width=\"2\" height=\"8\"/><rect x=\"6\" y=\"3\" width=\"2\" height=\"8\"/></g>\n  <g stroke=\"#2f3a2b\"><line x1=\"14\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"74\" y2=\"140\" stroke-width=\"5\"/><line x1=\"126\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"186\" y2=\"140\" stroke-width=\"5\"/><line x1=\"74\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"126\" y2=\"140\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"54\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"114\" stroke-width=\"5\"/><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"166\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"226\" stroke-width=\"5\"/><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"114\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"166\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/></g>\n  <!-- 9x -->\n  <clipPath id=\"gr-zoom-clip\"><circle cx=\"300\" cy=\"140\" r=\"86\"/></clipPath>\n  <circle cx=\"300\" cy=\"140\" r=\"86\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n  <g clip-path=\"url(#gr-zoom-clip)\"><g transform=\"translate(300 146) scale(3)\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"><ellipse rx=\"10\" ry=\"5\"/><circle cx=\"9\" cy=\"-6\" r=\"3.5\"/><rect x=\"-8\" y=\"3\" width=\"2\" height=\"8\"/><rect x=\"6\" y=\"3\" width=\"2\" height=\"8\"/></g></g>\n  <circle cx=\"300\" cy=\"140\" r=\"86\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <g stroke=\"#2f3a2b\"><line x1=\"214\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"274\" y2=\"140\" stroke-width=\"5\"/><line x1=\"326\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"386\" y2=\"140\" stroke-width=\"5\"/><line x1=\"274\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"326\" y2=\"140\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"300\" y1=\"54\" x2=\"300\" y2=\"114\" stroke-width=\"5\"/><line x1=\"300\" y1=\"166\" x2=\"300\" y2=\"226\" stroke-width=\"5\"/><line x1=\"300\" y1=\"114\" x2=\"300\" y2=\"166\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/></g>\n  <g font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\n    <text x=\"100\" y=\"252\">3x: wide view</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"252\">9x: big, narrow</text>\n  </g>\n  <g font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"100\" y=\"272\">close deer in timber</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"272\">plenty at 300 m</text></g>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>\"3 to 9x40\": zoom 3 to 9 times, 40 mm front lens <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>More zoom is not better. It shrinks your view (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: low power, high power, lens size</summary><ul><li>\"3 to 9x40\" means zoom 3 times to 9 times, with a 40 mm front lens <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Low power (2.5 to 3x) gives a wide view for close deer in timber <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>9 to 10x is plenty for a deer at 300 m <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Objective 40 to 44 mm is the sweet spot. Bigger sits higher and weighs more <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>More zoom is not better. It shrinks your view and adds weight (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation: zooming from 3 to 9 times power. In a second focal plane scope, the deer grows but the crosshair stays the same size. In a first focal plane scope, the deer and the crosshair grow together.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Zoom 3x to 9x</text>\n  <clipPath id=\"gr-focal-plane-c1\"><circle cx=\"100\" cy=\"140\" r=\"84\"/></clipPath>\n  <clipPath id=\"gr-focal-plane-c2\"><circle cx=\"300\" cy=\"140\" r=\"84\"/></clipPath>\n  <circle cx=\"100\" cy=\"140\" r=\"84\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/><circle cx=\"300\" cy=\"140\" r=\"84\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n  <g clip-path=\"url(#gr-focal-plane-c1)\"><g transform=\"translate(100 140)\"><g fill=\"#8b5a2b\">\n    <animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"scale\" values=\"1;3\" begin=\"1s\" dur=\"4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <ellipse rx=\"12\" ry=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"11\" cy=\"-7\" r=\"4\"/><rect x=\"-9\" y=\"3\" width=\"2.5\" height=\"10\"/><rect x=\"7\" y=\"3\" width=\"2.5\" height=\"10\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g stroke=\"#2f3a2b\"><line x1=\"-84\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"-30\" y2=\"0\" stroke-width=\"5\"/><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"84\" y2=\"0\" stroke-width=\"5\"/><line x1=\"-30\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"30\" y2=\"0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"-84\" x2=\"0\" y2=\"-30\" stroke-width=\"5\"/><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"0\" y2=\"84\" stroke-width=\"5\"/><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"-30\" x2=\"0\" y2=\"30\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/></g>\n  </g></g>\n  <g clip-path=\"url(#gr-focal-plane-c2)\"><g transform=\"translate(300 140)\"><g>\n    <animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"scale\" values=\"1;3\" begin=\"1s\" dur=\"4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <g fill=\"#8b5a2b\"><ellipse rx=\"12\" ry=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"11\" cy=\"-7\" r=\"4\"/><rect x=\"-9\" y=\"3\" width=\"2.5\" height=\"10\"/><rect x=\"7\" y=\"3\" width=\"2.5\" height=\"10\"/></g>\n    <g stroke=\"#2f3a2b\"><line x1=\"-84\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"-30\" y2=\"0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"30\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"84\" y2=\"0\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"-30\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"30\" y2=\"0\" stroke-width=\".6\"/><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"-84\" x2=\"0\" y2=\"-30\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"30\" x2=\"0\" y2=\"84\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"-30\" x2=\"0\" y2=\"30\" stroke-width=\".6\"/></g>\n  </g></g></g>\n  <circle cx=\"100\" cy=\"140\" r=\"84\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"300\" cy=\"140\" r=\"84\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <g font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"100\" y=\"250\">Second focal plane</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"250\">First focal plane</text></g>\n  <g font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"100\" y=\"270\">Crosshair stays same</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"270\">Crosshair grows</text></g>\n  <text x=\"100\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Simple: beginners</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"44\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">\n    <tspan>Power: 3x</tspan>\n    <set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\"/>\n  </text>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"5s\" dur=\".4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <rect x=\"160\" y=\"30\" width=\"80\" height=\"20\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"44\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Power: 9x</text>\n  </g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Watch the crosshair as the scope zooms. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Two reticles. Duplex: thick outer posts lead your eye to a thin centre crosshair, the simplest choice. BDC: extra hash marks below the centre for longer shots, useful only after you confirm drops on paper.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Reticles: what you see</text>\n  <circle cx=\"100\" cy=\"140\" r=\"86\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <g stroke=\"#2f3a2b\"><line x1=\"14\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"70\" y2=\"140\" stroke-width=\"6\"/><line x1=\"130\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"186\" y2=\"140\" stroke-width=\"6\"/><line x1=\"70\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"140\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"54\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"110\" stroke-width=\"6\"/><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"170\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"226\" stroke-width=\"6\"/><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"110\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"170\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/></g>\n  <circle cx=\"300\" cy=\"140\" r=\"86\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <g stroke=\"#2f3a2b\"><line x1=\"214\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"270\" y2=\"140\" stroke-width=\"6\"/><line x1=\"330\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"386\" y2=\"140\" stroke-width=\"6\"/><line x1=\"270\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"140\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"300\" y1=\"54\" x2=\"300\" y2=\"110\" stroke-width=\"6\"/><line x1=\"300\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"300\" y2=\"226\" stroke-width=\"6\"/><line x1=\"300\" y1=\"110\" x2=\"300\" y2=\"200\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/>\n    <line x1=\"290\" y1=\"156\" x2=\"310\" y2=\"156\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"288\" y1=\"172\" x2=\"312\" y2=\"172\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"286\" y1=\"188\" x2=\"314\" y2=\"188\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/></g>\n  <g font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#e8590c\" font-weight=\"bold\"><text x=\"316\" y=\"160\">200</text><text x=\"318\" y=\"176\">300</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"192\">400</text></g>\n  <g font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"100\" y=\"252\">Duplex</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"252\">BDC hash marks</text></g>\n  <g font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"100\" y=\"272\">Simplest. My lean</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"272\">Only after paper tests</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"290\">Example marks only</text></g>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Beginner pick: <strong>SFP</strong> (second focal plane) with a <strong>duplex</strong> crosshair <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: SFP, FFP, BDC explained</summary><ul><li>SFP (second focal plane): crosshair stays the same size when you zoom <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.<ul><li>Simple. Best for beginners. Hash marks are only true at one power <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul></li><li>FFP (first focal plane): crosshair grows with zoom. Marks are true at every power <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.<ul><li>Better for long range dialing. Thin crosshair at low power in dim light <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul></li><li>Reticle: <strong>duplex</strong> (thick outer posts, thin centre) is simplest <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>BDC (bullet drop compensator) hash marks help only after you confirm drops on paper <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>The distances on the BDC drawing are an example only. Every scope and load differs.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Elevation turret seen from above. The dial is marked UP with an arrow. Each click is one quarter MOA, about 0.73 centimetres at 100 metres. 4 clicks make 1 MOA, about 2.9 centimetres. Turn the dial the way the arrow shows to move the bullet. A cap screws on to stop bumps.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The turret, seen from above</text>\n  <circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"160\" r=\"96\" fill=\"#4a4f48\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"4\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"160\" r=\"70\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <g stroke=\"#fffaf0\" stroke-width=\"2\">\n    <line x1=\"120\" y1=\"66\" x2=\"120\" y2=\"86\"/><line x1=\"152\" y1=\"71\" x2=\"146\" y2=\"88\"/><line x1=\"181\" y1=\"88\" x2=\"170\" y2=\"102\"/><line x1=\"203\" y1=\"113\" x2=\"188\" y2=\"122\"/><line x1=\"214\" y1=\"144\" x2=\"198\" y2=\"148\"/>\n    <line x1=\"88\" y1=\"71\" x2=\"94\" y2=\"88\"/><line x1=\"59\" y1=\"88\" x2=\"70\" y2=\"102\"/><line x1=\"37\" y1=\"113\" x2=\"52\" y2=\"122\"/><line x1=\"26\" y1=\"144\" x2=\"42\" y2=\"148\"/>\n  </g>\n  <text x=\"120\" y=\"122\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">UP</text>\n  <path d=\"M92 150 A 34 34 0 0 1 148 150\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"4\"/>\n  <path d=\"M140 140 l10 12 l4 -15\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"4\"/>\n  <text x=\"120\" y=\"190\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1/4 MOA</text>\n  <text x=\"120\" y=\"208\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" text-anchor=\"middle\">per click</text>\n  <g font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">\n    <text x=\"236\" y=\"76\">1 click</text><text x=\"236\" y=\"96\" fill=\"#e8590c\">0.73 cm at 100 m</text>\n    <text x=\"236\" y=\"136\">4 clicks = 1 MOA</text><text x=\"236\" y=\"156\" fill=\"#e8590c\">2.9 cm at 100 m</text>\n    <text x=\"236\" y=\"196\">Turn the way</text><text x=\"236\" y=\"216\">you want the</text><text x=\"236\" y=\"236\">bullet to go</text>\n  </g>\n  <text x=\"236\" y=\"276\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Capped turrets: no bumps</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>1 click = 1/4 MOA (minute of angle), about 0.73 cm at 100 m (70 to 85%).</li></ul><ul><li>Eye relief 9 cm (3.5 in) or more. A .308 kicks <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: turrets, eye relief, parallax</summary><ul><li><strong>Turrets:</strong> the knobs that move the crosshair. Capped turrets cannot get bumped in the bush <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.<ul><li>Most hunting scopes move 1/4 MOA per click <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>. Session 5 has the math.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Eye relief:</strong> distance from your eye to the rear lens for a full picture <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.<ul><li>Look for about 9 cm (3.5 in) or more. A .308 kicks, and short eye relief cuts your brow <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Parallax:</strong> the crosshair seems to shift if your eye is off centre <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.<ul><li>Fixed at 100 yd (91 m) is fine for hunting out to about 300 m <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul></li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 400\" font-family=\"sans-serif\">\n  <defs>\n    <marker id=\"er-arrow\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"8\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto-start-reverse\">\n      <path d=\"M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n    </marker>\n  </defs>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"400\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Eye relief and sight clearance</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"46\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Side view, not to scale</text>\n\n  <!-- stock -->\n  <path d=\"M120,262 L120,292 L60,330 L20,330 L20,300 L70,282 Z\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <!-- receiver -->\n  <rect x=\"120\" y=\"250\" width=\"140\" height=\"36\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <!-- barrel -->\n  <rect x=\"260\" y=\"258\" width=\"130\" height=\"14\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <!-- rail -->\n  <rect x=\"170\" y=\"242\" width=\"80\" height=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n  <!-- rear drum sight -->\n  <circle cx=\"142\" cy=\"236\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#6b4f35\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <!-- rings -->\n  <rect x=\"180\" y=\"196\" width=\"12\" height=\"46\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n  <rect x=\"232\" y=\"196\" width=\"12\" height=\"46\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n  <!-- scope -->\n  <rect x=\"100\" y=\"180\" width=\"230\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#23261f\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n  <path d=\"M100,172 L80,170 L80,206 L100,204 Z\" fill=\"#23261f\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n  <path d=\"M300,180 L330,166 L362,166 L362,210 L330,210 L300,196 Z\" fill=\"#23261f\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n  <rect x=\"204\" y=\"162\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" fill=\"#23261f\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n  <text x=\"250\" y=\"156\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" font-weight=\"bold\">Scope</text>\n  <!-- eye -->\n  <ellipse cx=\"34\" cy=\"188\" rx=\"12\" ry=\"8\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"38\" cy=\"188\" r=\"4\" fill=\"#23261f\"/>\n  <text x=\"34\" y=\"168\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#23261f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Eye</text>\n  <!-- eye relief arrow -->\n  <line x1=\"48\" y1=\"126\" x2=\"78\" y2=\"126\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" marker-start=\"url(#er-arrow)\" marker-end=\"url(#er-arrow)\"/>\n  <line x1=\"46\" y1=\"118\" x2=\"46\" y2=\"180\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/>\n  <line x1=\"80\" y1=\"118\" x2=\"80\" y2=\"168\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/>\n  <text x=\"20\" y=\"96\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" font-weight=\"bold\">Eye relief</text>\n  <text x=\"20\" y=\"114\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">about 9 to 10 cm (3.5 to 4 in)</text>\n  <!-- clearance arrow -->\n  <line x1=\"142\" y1=\"199\" x2=\"142\" y2=\"219\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" marker-start=\"url(#er-arrow)\" marker-end=\"url(#er-arrow)\"/>\n  <text x=\"20\" y=\"362\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" font-weight=\"bold\">Gap: scope must clear</text>\n  <text x=\"20\" y=\"382\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" font-weight=\"bold\">the rear drum sight</text>\n  <text x=\"96\" y=\"216\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#e8590c\" font-weight=\"bold\">Gap</text>\n  <text x=\"10\" y=\"252\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">Rear drum sight</text>\n  <text x=\"320\" y=\"296\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">Barrel</text>\n  <text x=\"190\" y=\"328\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#23261f\">Rings on short rail</text>\n  <line x1=\"212\" y1=\"314\" x2=\"212\" y2=\"252\" stroke=\"#23261f\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/>\n</svg>\n</figure>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Your Tikka T3x Arctic has a tall rear drum sight on the receiver. With low rings, the scope hits the drum. With high rings, the scope clears it. Dry fit at the store before you pay.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Clear the rear drum sight</text>\n  <!-- low rings -->\n  <text x=\"20\" y=\"54\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\">Low rings ✗</text>\n  <rect x=\"20\" y=\"110\" width=\"340\" height=\"18\" fill=\"#6b6f68\"/><rect x=\"110\" y=\"102\" width=\"70\" height=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"80\" y=\"84\" width=\"22\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><text x=\"91\" y=\"146\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Drum</text>\n  <path d=\"M30 80 L60 84 L60 98 L30 102 Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"60\" y=\"84\" width=\"96\" height=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M156 84 L176 72 L210 72 L210 110 L176 110 L156 98 Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" opacity=\".85\"/>\n  <g fill=\"#8a9a6b\"><rect x=\"114\" y=\"82\" width=\"10\" height=\"22\"/><rect x=\"164\" y=\"80\" width=\"10\" height=\"24\"/></g>\n  <circle cx=\"91\" cy=\"84\" r=\"12\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <text x=\"232\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\">Scope hits it</text>\n  <!-- high rings -->\n  <text x=\"20\" y=\"182\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f6b3a\">High rings ✓</text>\n  <rect x=\"20\" y=\"250\" width=\"340\" height=\"18\" fill=\"#6b6f68\"/><rect x=\"110\" y=\"242\" width=\"70\" height=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"80\" y=\"224\" width=\"22\" height=\"26\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n  <path d=\"M30 194 L60 198 L60 212 L30 216 Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"60\" y=\"198\" width=\"96\" height=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M156 198 L176 186 L210 186 L210 224 L176 224 L156 212 Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" opacity=\".85\"/>\n  <g fill=\"#8a9a6b\"><rect x=\"114\" y=\"196\" width=\"10\" height=\"46\"/><rect x=\"164\" y=\"196\" width=\"10\" height=\"46\"/></g>\n  <text x=\"232\" y=\"214\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f6b3a\">Clears the drum</text>\n  <text x=\"232\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Dry fit at the store</text>\n  <text x=\"300\" y=\"148\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Receiver and rail</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Bring the rifle to the store. <strong>Dry fit</strong> scope and rings before you pay (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: rail, sight and ring notes</summary><ul><li>20 inch stainless barrel, 1 in 11 twist, removable rail <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>Rail is short, about 12 to 13 cm (4.75 to 5 in), to make room for the rear sight <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Rear sight is a rotary drum peep sight, 100 to 600 m <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>Owners report <strong>high rings</strong> needed to clear the drum with a 40 to 44 mm scope <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li>A cantilever mount clears the drum but puts the scope high <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li>Some owners remove the irons. Removing them yourself: <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span> with a gunsmith <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li>Rail type (Picatinny or Weaver slots): <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span> at the store.</li><li>Dry fit: check clearance over the drum, and that the rings land on the scope tube, not on the turret or bells (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Scope</th><th>Tube</th><th>CAD price</th><th>Certainty</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Vortex Diamondback 3 to 9x40</td><td>1 in</td><td>$270 to $400</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Burris Fullfield E1 3 to 9x40</td><td>1 in</td><td>$340 to $390</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Leupold VX Freedom 3 to 9x40</td><td>1 in</td><td>$472 to $690</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: eye relief and price note</summary><ul><li>Eye relief: Diamondback about 3.3 to 3.5 in. VX Freedom about 3.66 to 4.17 in, 12.2 oz <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>CAD (Canadian dollars). Price checked 2026-10-01. Search preview prices, verify at checkout.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Scope</th><th>Tube</th><th>CAD price</th><th>Certainty</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Burris Signature HD 3 to 15x44</td><td>30 mm</td><td>$765 to $840</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Leupold VX 3HD 3.5 to 10x40</td><td>1 in</td><td>$835 to $1,006</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Vortex Viper HD 3 to 15x44</td><td>30 mm</td><td>$1,099 to $1,199</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Zeiss Conquest V4 4 to 16x44</td><td>30 mm</td><td>$1,125 to $1,300</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: eye relief and price note</summary><ul><li>VX 3HD 3.5 to 10x40: eye relief about 3.6 to 4.4 in, 13.5 oz <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Viper HD 3 to 15x44: about 3.4 in eye relief, about 22 oz <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>CAD (Canadian dollars). Price checked 2026-10-01. Search preview prices, verify at checkout.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Scope</th><th>Tube</th><th>CAD price</th><th>Certainty</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Leupold VX 5HD 3 to 15x44</td><td>30 mm</td><td>$1,700 to $2,500</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Swarovski Z5 3.5 to 18x44</td><td>1 in</td><td>$1,879 to $2,139</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Zeiss Conquest V6 2 to 12x50</td><td>30 mm</td><td>about $3,300, one source</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: notes</summary><ul><li>Confirm the tube size on the box before you buy rings (Tip).</li><li>Premium glass is brighter in the last minutes of legal light. It does not shoot straighter (Tip).</li><li>CAD (Canadian dollars). Price checked 2026-10-01. Search preview prices, verify at checkout.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Rings</th><th>Size</th><th>CAD price</th><th>Certainty</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Leupold Rifleman</td><td>1 in</td><td>$34</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Burris Signature Zee</td><td>30 mm</td><td>$63 to $100</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Vortex Pro</td><td>30 mm</td><td>$119 to $130</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Warne Mountain Tech</td><td>1 in</td><td>from $205</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Nightforce Ultralite</td><td>30 mm</td><td>$236 to $264</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Ring size = scope tube: <strong>1 inch or 30 mm</strong> <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: ring height and price note</summary><ul><li>Ring size must match the scope tube: <strong>1 inch or 30 mm</strong> <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Ring height: with the rear sight on, expect <strong>high</strong> for a 40 to 44 mm scope <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>. Irons off: low or medium <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span>.</li><li>CAD (Canadian dollars). Price checked 2026-10-01. Search preview prices, verify at checkout.</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"steps\" data-n=\"6\"><div class=\"steps-head\"><b>Mount the scope in 6 steps</b><span class=\"steps-count\">1 of 6</span></div><div class=\"steps-track\"><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Step 1: the rifle sits in a rest, pointed a safe way. The bolt is out and lies beside it. Look in the chamber and magazine well: empty.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bolt out. Empty.</text>\n  <path d=\"M20 120 L130 112 L140 112 L150 140 L250 138 L250 150 L140 156 L118 168 L104 160 L20 176 Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <rect x=\"130\" y=\"102\" width=\"80\" height=\"20\" fill=\"#6b6f68\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <rect x=\"210\" y=\"106\" width=\"176\" height=\"9\" fill=\"#6b6f68\"/>\n  <rect x=\"150\" y=\"104\" width=\"40\" height=\"10\" fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <path d=\"M150 156 q 2 16 22 14 l2 -14\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <!-- bolt -->\n  <rect x=\"120\" y=\"214\" width=\"120\" height=\"14\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#6b6f68\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <path d=\"M130 228 l-8 22\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"5\"/><circle cx=\"121\" cy=\"253\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <path d=\"M170 140 L180 200\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\"/><path d=\"M172 194 l8 10 l4 -12\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <text x=\"260\" y=\"226\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Bolt</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"90\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Look: chamber and magazine empty</text>\n  <text x=\"380\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"end\">Muzzle safe way</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>1.</b> Prove it unloaded. Bolt out.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Step 2: close up of the rail on top of the receiver. Clean and degrease it. Set two ring bases in the slots and push each one forward, toward the muzzle.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Ring bases on the rail</text>\n  <rect x=\"30\" y=\"170\" width=\"340\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#6b6f68\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <rect x=\"40\" y=\"150\" width=\"320\" height=\"20\" fill=\"#4a4f48\"/>\n  <g fill=\"#fffaf0\"><rect x=\"60\" y=\"150\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\"/><rect x=\"100\" y=\"150\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\"/><rect x=\"140\" y=\"150\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\"/><rect x=\"180\" y=\"150\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\"/><rect x=\"220\" y=\"150\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\"/><rect x=\"260\" y=\"150\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\"/><rect x=\"300\" y=\"150\" width=\"12\" height=\"12\"/></g>\n  <g fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path d=\"M110 150 L110 104 Q 130 92 150 104 L150 150 Z\"/><path d=\"M270 150 L270 104 Q 290 92 310 104 L310 150 Z\"/></g>\n  <g stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"4\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M160 120 h40 m-10 -8 l10 8 l-10 8\"/><path d=\"M320 120 h40 m-10 -8 l10 8 l-10 8\"/></g>\n  <text x=\"340\" y=\"80\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Push</text><text x=\"340\" y=\"98\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">forward</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"240\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Clean and degrease rail and screws first</text>\n  <text x=\"380\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"end\">Muzzle this way →</text>\n  <text x=\"20\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Tip</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>2.</b> Clean the rail. Push ring bases forward in the slots.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Step 3: lay the scope in the bottom ring halves. Put the ring caps on loosely so the scope can still slide.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Scope in, caps loose</text>\n  <rect x=\"30\" y=\"220\" width=\"340\" height=\"24\" fill=\"#6b6f68\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <g fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"><path d=\"M110 220 L110 178 L150 178 L150 220 Z\"/><path d=\"M260 220 L260 178 L300 178 L300 220 Z\"/></g>\n  <path d=\"M30 150 L70 156 L70 184 L30 190 Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"70\" y=\"156\" width=\"240\" height=\"26\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><path d=\"M310 156 L340 140 L380 140 L380 196 L340 196 L310 182 Z\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <g fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" opacity=\".9\"><path d=\"M110 132 L150 132 L150 146 L110 146 Z\"/><path d=\"M260 132 L300 132 L300 146 L260 146 Z\"/></g>\n  <g stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"><line x1=\"130\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"156\"/><line x1=\"280\" y1=\"146\" x2=\"280\" y2=\"156\"/></g>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Caps on loosely</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"276\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Bottom ring halves hold the tube</text>\n  <path d=\"M60 120 h-30 m8 -6 l-8 6 l8 6 M330 120 h30 m-8 -6 l8 6 l-8 6\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Still slides</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>3.</b> Lay the scope in the bottom rings. Caps loose.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Step 4: set eye relief. Rifle at your shoulder, scope on highest power. A black ring around the view means move the scope. Slide it until you see the full picture, then 1 centimetre more forward.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Set eye relief</text>\n  <circle cx=\"100\" cy=\"130\" r=\"66\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><circle cx=\"100\" cy=\"130\" r=\"34\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"300\" cy=\"130\" r=\"66\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <g stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><line x1=\"66\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"134\" y2=\"130\"/><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"96\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"164\"/><line x1=\"234\" y1=\"130\" x2=\"366\" y2=\"130\"/><line x1=\"300\" y1=\"64\" x2=\"300\" y2=\"196\"/></g>\n  <g font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"100\" y=\"222\" fill=\"#c0392b\">Black ring ✗</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"222\" fill=\"#2f6b3a\">Full picture ✓</text></g>\n  <g font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"100\" y=\"242\">slide the scope</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"242\">then 1 cm forward</text></g>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Highest power, rifle at your shoulder</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>4.</b> Slide for a full picture, then 1 cm forward.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Step 5: level the crosshair to the rifle, not to the floor. Seen from behind, the vertical crosshair lines up with the centre line of the rifle.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Level to the rifle</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"48\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">View from behind the rifle</text>\n  <circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"120\" r=\"54\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <g stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"><line x1=\"146\" y1=\"120\" x2=\"254\" y2=\"120\"/><line x1=\"200\" y1=\"66\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"174\"/></g>\n  <rect x=\"180\" y=\"174\" width=\"40\" height=\"24\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <rect x=\"172\" y=\"198\" width=\"56\" height=\"40\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#6b6f68\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <path d=\"M184 238 L176 286 L224 286 L216 238 Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <line x1=\"200\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"200\" y2=\"292\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\"/>\n  <text x=\"300\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">Rifle centre</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"170\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">line</text>\n  <text x=\"20\" y=\"150\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Crosshair</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"170\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">straight up</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>5.</b> Level the crosshair to the rifle.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Step 6: ring cap seen from above with 4 screws. Tighten a little at a time in a cross pattern: 1, 2, 3, 4. Keep the gaps even on both sides. Finish with a torque wrench to the ring maker's number, then a paint pen line across each screw.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Tighten in a cross</text>\n  <rect x=\"40\" y=\"110\" width=\"200\" height=\"40\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"100\" y=\"70\" width=\"80\" height=\"120\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <g fill=\"#fffaf0\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"><circle cx=\"118\" cy=\"88\" r=\"9\"/><circle cx=\"162\" cy=\"172\" r=\"9\"/><circle cx=\"162\" cy=\"88\" r=\"9\"/><circle cx=\"118\" cy=\"172\" r=\"9\"/></g>\n  <g stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\"><line x1=\"112\" y1=\"88\" x2=\"124\" y2=\"88\"/><line x1=\"156\" y1=\"172\" x2=\"168\" y2=\"172\"/><line x1=\"156\" y1=\"88\" x2=\"168\" y2=\"88\"/><line x1=\"112\" y1=\"172\" x2=\"124\" y2=\"172\"/></g>\n  <g font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\"><text x=\"84\" y=\"94\">1</text><text x=\"176\" y=\"178\">2</text><text x=\"176\" y=\"94\">3</text><text x=\"84\" y=\"178\">4</text></g>\n  <path d=\"M126 96 L154 164 M154 96 L126 164\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 4\"/>\n  <!-- torque wrench -->\n  <rect x=\"262\" y=\"96\" width=\"110\" height=\"18\" rx=\"9\" fill=\"#6b6f68\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"268\" cy=\"105\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#6b6f68\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <text x=\"316\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Torque wrench</text>\n  <text x=\"316\" y=\"158\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">to the maker's number</text>\n  <text x=\"140\" y=\"222\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Even gaps both sides</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Paint pen line on each screw</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"282\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A broken line means it moved</text>\n</svg>\n<figcaption><b>6.</b> Tighten in a cross. Torque to the maker's number.</figcaption></figure></div><div class=\"steps-nav\"><button class=\"steps-prev\" aria-label=\"Back\">‹ Back</button><span class=\"steps-dots\"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><button class=\"steps-next\" aria-label=\"Next\">Next ›</button></div></div><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the full steps and torque table</summary><ol><li>Prove the rifle unloaded. Bolt out (<button class=\"term\" data-term=\"ACTS\">ACTS</button>).</li><li>Clean and degrease rail, ring bases and screws (Tip).</li><li>Fit ring bases to the rail. Push them forward in the slots, toward the muzzle (Tip).</li><li>Lay the scope in the bottom ring halves. Caps on loosely.</li><li>Set eye relief: rifle at your shoulder, scope on highest power, slide it until the full picture appears. Then 1 cm more forward (Tip).</li><li>Level the crosshair to the rifle, not to the floor (Tip).</li><li>Tighten cap screws a little at a time, in a cross pattern. Keep the gaps even on both sides (Tip).</li><li>Torque to the ring maker's number with a torque wrench.</li></ol><div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Rings</th><th>Maker torque</th><th>Certainty</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Vortex Pro</td><td>Caps 18 in lb, cross bolt 65 in lb</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Burris Signature Zee</td><td>Caps 20 in lb, cross bolt 30 in lb</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Leupold (standard rings)</td><td>Ring screws up to 28 in lb. Varies by model</td><td><span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span></td></tr></tbody></table></div><ul><li>Use the number on <strong>your</strong> ring maker's sheet. Too tight can crush a scope tube. Too loose and the scope moves after a few shots.</li></ul></details><aside class=\"callout lean\"><div class=\"callout-t\">My lean (opinion)</div><p><strong>Leupold VX Freedom 3 to 9x40</strong> in high 1 inch rings. About $500 to $725 with rings. Want brighter glass for about $350 more? Leupold VX 3HD 3.5 to 10x40.</p></aside>","<aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>A scope you can't trust is worse than iron sights. Mount it right, mark the screws, check them.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout mistake\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Rings bought before checking drum clearance.</li><li>Scope too far back. The .308 bites your eyebrow.</li><li>Ring screws cranked with no torque wrench.</li></ul></aside><aside class=\"callout field\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>Paint pen line across each ring screw head. A broken line means a screw moved.</p></aside>","<ul><li>Rifle data, owner reports, torque specs and prices: secondary sources and maker pages (60 to 80%).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: all sources</summary><ul><li><a href=\"https://www.all4shooters.com/en/hunting/rifles/tikka-t3x-arctic-bolt-action-in-308-winchester-features-test/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">all4shooters Tikka T3x Arctic test</a>, rear drum sight 100 to 600 m, checked 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span></li><li><a href=\"https://www.recoilweb.com/tikka-t3x-arctic-131608.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Recoil Magazine Tikka T3x Arctic review</a>, rail and cantilever clearance, checked 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span></li><li><a href=\"https://www.canadiangunnutz.com/forum/threads/tikka-t3x-arctic-scope-mounting-options.2251408/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Canadian Gun Nutz: T3x Arctic scope mounting options</a>, owner reports, checked 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">60%</span></li><li>Sako Tikka T3x Arctic product data via gear research 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span></li><li><a href=\"https://vortexoptics.com/blog/how-to-torque-your-riflescope-rings.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Vortex: how to torque your riflescope rings</a>, checked 2026-10-01 (70%, search preview)</li><li><a href=\"https://burris.supportsync.com/articles/view/torque-specs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Burris torque specs</a>, checked 2026-10-01 (65%, search preview)</li><li><a href=\"https://www.leupold.com/media/manuals/std_mounting_instructions.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Leupold standard rings mounting instructions</a>, checked 2026-10-01 (60%, search preview, values vary by product)</li><li>Scope and ring prices: search previews of Canadian retailers, price checked 2026-10-01 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span></li></ul></details>"]